1968.

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:30.510
this room.

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:31.340
Okay.

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:34.920
So let's get down to the infighting.

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:39.250
You have been a thorn in my side for years, Straker.

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:45.040
Consistently excessive demands for the diversion of resources to your organization.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:48.480
Now you're saying a total clearance program.

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:49.130
Right.

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:50.360
And I'm saying.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.440
While I'm running this commission.

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:55.450
I'll fight you on this issue every inch of the way.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:18.080
you've been practicing.

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:21.200
What are you working on anyway, Alec?

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:23.560
one of Stryker's projects.

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:26.130
It's a beautification campaign.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:28.200
But I won't deny you could use it.

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:29.920
Space

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:30.220
junk

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.330
Straker wants it all cleared.

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:36.140
Well, the Astrophysical Commission takes care of any space junk.

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:38.490
Anything that has a potential?

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.060
Straker has an idea could be used by the aliens to crack our defense system.

00:06:43.690 --> 00:06:45.050
I'm beginning to think he may be onto something.

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:47.660
Well, if your report shows it's a possibility.

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:49.490
The junk gets cleared.

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:50.940
So what's the problem?

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:53.670
James L. Henderson is the problem.

00:06:54.090 --> 00:06:54.530
Cast.

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:55.400
Time.

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:56.360
Personnel.

00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:57.070
Resources.

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:00.000
You want.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:00.420
No wonder reasons.

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:01.610
Why not?

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:05.440
I can give you a hundred.

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:06.620
Listen, Henderson.

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:10.470
Every item of space junk could be cleared in a matter of weeks.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.730
If the commission gave its full support.

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:14.520
Cost?

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:16.080
I admit, it would be high.

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:18.670
But safety factors alone would justify it.

00:07:19.610 --> 00:07:20.370
safety factors.

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:21.310
Yes.

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:24.200
My organization uses space more than any other.

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:28.900
My pilots take more risks with that junk in one month than my men do in a year.

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:34.820
No, we need fat stringer.

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:36.590
Details, statistics.

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:38.580
You just don't have them.

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:39.330
Don't I?

00:07:39.970 --> 00:07:40.870
Of course you don't.

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:41.850
I have my report.

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:43.980
Your report.

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:49.740
You promised that the commission would not take a final decision on the clearance program until my report had been fully considered.

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:50.790
And so it won't.

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:56.680
However, I must confess, I don't think it'll have that much influence.

00:07:57.930 --> 00:07:59.230
Well, if that's so, Henderson...

00:07:59.300 --> 00:07:59.980
It must be big.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.740
because you've already swung the commission against it.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:02.540
Look, Straker.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:07.040
We've just completed the annual clearance of all items of space junk we consider a menace to navigation.

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:10.060
The cost was more than double that of last year's operation.

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:11.400
And worth every penny.

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:16.470
Do you realize what a full clearance program would cost?

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:17.380
Look.

00:08:18.070 --> 00:08:19.830
I'm not going to swap dollar signs with you, Henderson.

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:21.300
Men's lives are at stake.

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:23.560
Now, I want that junk cleared.

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:25.720
Every last piece.

00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:55.050
on his way, sir.

00:08:59.050 --> 00:08:59.570
the straight cut.

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:04.000
Freeman.

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:05.340
Alec.

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:07.200
I want that space clearance report.

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:08.500
Well, he just got here.

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:09.770
And there's data still missing.

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:11.090
I don't care what's missing.

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:16.590
Looks like Henderson's commission have already decided against a major space clearance project.

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:18.670
We have to convince them otherwise.

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:21.300
Well, give me 24 hours. It can't make any difference to you.

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:23.060
But it could make a heck of a difference to the report.

00:09:23.240 --> 00:09:24.540
I want that report, Alec.

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:27.300
I don't care what shape it's in, just get it back here.

00:09:32.870 --> 00:09:33.850
Thank you.

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:47.640
Shadow Lunar Module 32 cleared for takeoff at 14.21.34.

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:48.670
Stand by.

00:09:49.640 --> 00:09:50.400
Roger, moon base.

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:52.030
Confirm T.E.T.

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:53.340
Affirmative.

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:55.470
Trans-Earth trajectory green.

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:04.200
Lift off, 32.

00:10:23.770 --> 00:10:24.650
Check delta coordinates.

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:28.600
Coordinates correct, sir.

00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:36.720
Earth orbit insertion, 2 hours 13 minutes 8 seconds, sir.

00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:37.980
Right.

00:11:26.420 --> 00:11:27.380
HQ and Moonbase.

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:29.900
And then we're going for EOI.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.920
in 43 minutes 29 seconds.

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:33.480
Right, sir.

00:11:35.770 --> 00:11:40.030
32 reports Earth orbit insertion at 13.0821, sir.

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:41.220
Contact SID.

00:11:41.480 --> 00:11:42.660
Tracking procedure green.

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:44.880
Has Shadow HQ been alert?

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:45.840
Yes, sir.

00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:49.020
So everything's fine?

00:11:49.880 --> 00:11:50.780
Straker's not gonna think so.

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:52.220
He's expecting you.

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:11.620
Reentry angle.

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:13.580
six decimal, 58 degrees.

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:17.740
DOI.

00:12:17.980 --> 00:12:18.400
Four minutes.

00:12:19.190 --> 00:12:19.570
15 seconds.

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:30.910
Sighting, sir.

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:32.640
at 7035.

00:12:34.470 --> 00:12:35.430
That's in behind us.

00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:37.180
Confirm sighting.

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:39.370
affirmative, sir.

00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:40.780
And it's closing fast.

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:43.160
Contact Moonbase.

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:48.730
32 reports unidentified sightings, sir.

00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:50.030
Signal red alert.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:51.480
Thank you.

00:13:02.230 --> 00:13:02.810
Thank you.

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:15.950
happening.

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:17.310
Angle increasing.

00:13:24.790 --> 00:13:25.950
The angle of re-entry is too steep.

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:28.930
Telling to correct angle of re-entry.

00:13:31.270 --> 00:13:32.190
Lots of signals, huh?

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:35.760
It's still increasing.

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:37.390
Something's pulling us off course.

00:13:43.980 --> 00:13:44.660
We've got to correct.

00:13:59.210 --> 00:13:59.770
Which actuator?

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:01.650
One decimal three, burn.

00:14:05.600 --> 00:14:06.900
Thorboard insertion now.

00:14:11.860 --> 00:14:13.520
Response, they're in trouble.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:00.480
Look, Henderson.

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:02.830
All I need is another 48 hours.

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:04.600
Another 48 hours.

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:05.000
Yes.

00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:08.440
I can have a summary of the completed report on your desk by then.

00:15:09.850 --> 00:15:11.950
You know I can't hold up the commission any longer.

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:16.160
Why don't you let me tell them that you decided to withdraw your proposal?

00:15:18.740 --> 00:15:19.460
I get you off the hook.

00:15:21.140 --> 00:15:22.480
I intend to hold you to your word.

00:15:22.970 --> 00:15:25.730
to consider my report before making a decision on the clearance program.

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:28.610
All right, Straker, I think I'm reading you.

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:30.000
You want.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.800
I want an alibi for that pilot of yours who killed himself and his crewman.

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:35.580
You want to blame it on the presence of unclear junk.

00:15:37.930 --> 00:15:39.170
I want your word, Henderson.

00:15:40.420 --> 00:15:41.200
And one condition.

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:48.850
Now, you consider your spacecraft was involved in a re-entry collision with an item of space junk?

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:50.100
It's a possibility.

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:50.870
Oh.

00:15:51.910 --> 00:15:52.570
A possibility.

00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:53.770
Yes.

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:57.500
So you suspend all lunar flights until we've...

00:15:57.580 --> 00:15:59.120
Fully investigated the...

00:15:59.720 --> 00:15:59.940
And

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:02.400
You realize what you're doing?

00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:04.000
Yes, Commander, I do.

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:08.780
I'm proving to the Commission that your organization in its present form

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:11.780
is an expensive and unworkable luxury.

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:23.800
Miss Eland.

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:29.420
I'm always hard at it. Sometimes you notice.

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:31.570
How did it go sir?

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:36.740
You know the code word Washington Square, Miss Eland.

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:39.740
Not without looking it up. It's not one we use regularly.

00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:41.240
Thank you.

00:16:41.510 --> 00:16:42.870
It's one I thought we'd never use.

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:44.740
What does it mean, sir?

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:46.840
It means shut down.

00:16:47.660 --> 00:16:48.740
Cancel lunar flights.

00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:51.210
Virtual isolation of moon base.

00:16:51.880 --> 00:16:52.860
Thank you.

00:17:10.100 --> 00:17:11.980
to all unit commanders, Washington Square.

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:12.980
I say again.

00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:14.450
Washington Square.

00:17:15.420 --> 00:17:15.560
Thank you.

00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:16.580
Compliance.

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:17.500
Washington Square.

00:17:18.230 --> 00:17:18.450
You

00:17:22.740 --> 00:17:23.240
Colonel Foster

00:17:23.860 --> 00:17:24.860
Sorry to disturb you, sir.

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:26.140
Code message from the shadow.

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:27.850
Washington Square

00:17:28.570 --> 00:17:29.310
I'll check it right away.

00:17:32.970 --> 00:17:33.590
There's no need.

00:17:34.380 --> 00:17:35.240
It means shut down.

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:36.180
What?

00:17:37.990 --> 00:17:41.070
More specifically, it involves a complete ban on all orbital flights.

00:17:55.210 --> 00:17:55.970
Freeman for you.

00:17:57.670 --> 00:17:58.030
Put him on.

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:02.280
Why the ban on moon flight?

00:18:02.900 --> 00:18:03.240
Henderson

00:18:03.670 --> 00:18:04.070
But why?

00:18:04.410 --> 00:18:05.090
What about the report?

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:06.100
Forget it.

00:18:06.970 --> 00:18:10.530
The commissioner are going to believe that it's an attempt to blame space junk on the Maddox crash.

00:18:11.410 --> 00:18:12.930
when in fact you think it was...

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:13.540
Maddox.

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:14.920
Pilot error.

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:18.440
Take a rest. Enjoy the scenery, Alec.

00:18:23.860 --> 00:18:24.840
What's Straker trying to do?

00:18:26.390 --> 00:18:26.710
or not.

00:18:29.020 --> 00:18:30.000
It doesn't usually take a thing like that.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.620
laying down.

00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:32.340
You couldn't call it typical.

00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:35.300
And then there's Malik's.

00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:37.340
What do we do about him?

00:18:38.310 --> 00:18:38.930
Did you forget all about it?

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:40.010
What else can we do?

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:41.650
Any pilot can make a mistake.

00:18:42.540 --> 00:18:43.420
And you're only allowed one.

00:18:44.170 --> 00:18:45.050
No, Steve Maddox.

00:18:45.230 --> 00:18:45.650
Anyone.

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:48.390
a mistake. Not Steve Maddox. He's too experienced.

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:52.440
caused the re-entry error.

00:18:53.320 --> 00:18:56.100
...reported an unidentified sighting just before loss of signal.

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:57.890
But the trackers couldn't pick up anything.

00:18:59.020 --> 00:18:59.880
Well, it must have been something.

00:19:01.210 --> 00:19:01.830
Spacestep.

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:06.860
Maybe.

00:19:08.630 --> 00:19:08.970
Maybe.

00:19:10.740 --> 00:19:12.280
And we just sit back and do nothing about it?

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:12.660
No.

00:19:13.910 --> 00:19:15.110
We make sure it doesn't happen again.

00:19:24.570 --> 00:19:26.110
Get me 32's electronic log.

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:27.740
Captain Maddox, flight.

00:19:28.410 --> 00:19:28.730
Yes.

00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:11.400
What's going on here?

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:15.500
What the devil's going on?

00:20:15.800 --> 00:20:16.460
Who's in that module?

00:20:16.950 --> 00:20:17.570
Colonel Foster.

00:20:18.460 --> 00:20:19.300
Why didn't you tell me?

00:20:21.210 --> 00:20:21.690
Any of you.

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:23.990
Colonel Foster's orders.

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:26.790
On no account will we tell you until take-off was imminent.

00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:28.210
and irreversible.

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:31.340
Paul, cut your motors.

00:20:35.110 --> 00:20:36.350
I said cut your motors.

00:20:39.690 --> 00:20:40.430
This won't help.

00:20:41.480 --> 00:20:41.940
Spotlight.

00:20:42.410 --> 00:20:43.130
Taking out a module.

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:45.720
If you're doing it for the reasons I think you are.

00:20:46.660 --> 00:20:48.240
I'm going to fly the same course Maddox flew.

00:20:48.970 --> 00:20:50.470
under precisely the same conditions.

00:20:50.670 --> 00:20:50.970
Yes.

00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:51.960
You're crazy.

00:20:52.900 --> 00:20:53.600
What will it prove?

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:57.310
For one thing, Maddox wasn't responsible for the loss of his ship.

00:21:01.830 --> 00:21:02.870
Depends on how I get through.

00:21:04.020 --> 00:21:04.480
And if you don't.

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:06.880
Then I don't.

00:21:31.940 --> 00:21:32.100
Roger.

00:21:34.730 --> 00:21:35.030
three

00:21:36.170 --> 00:21:36.450
Roger.

00:21:45.420 --> 00:21:45.840
What is it?

00:21:52.900 --> 00:21:53.700
calling Moonbase.

00:21:56.390 --> 00:21:56.810
So far?

00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:03.940
EOI in two hours, 38 minutes, 22 seconds.

00:22:04.310 --> 00:22:04.610
project.

00:22:05.300 --> 00:22:06.540
Have you contacted Straker yet?

00:22:07.060 --> 00:22:07.360
No.

00:22:09.080 --> 00:22:10.980
But I have a feeling he'll be contacting me soon.

00:22:12.310 --> 00:22:13.510
sighting at galactic latitude.

00:22:14.740 --> 00:22:15.340
Forty-three.

00:22:15.860 --> 00:22:16.380
decimal

00:22:17.110 --> 00:22:17.670
One seven.

00:22:19.320 --> 00:22:19.780
Longitude

00:22:20.500 --> 00:22:21.780
14 that's all

00:22:22.490 --> 00:22:23.110
5-3

00:22:24.890 --> 00:22:26.350
But that's moon-based operations area.

00:22:26.490 --> 00:22:27.550
Right, call Commander Straker.

00:22:40.650 --> 00:22:41.750
is back right now.

00:22:44.300 --> 00:22:46.060
DOI in one hour precisely.

00:22:48.680 --> 00:22:49.540
We've gone too far for that.

00:22:50.410 --> 00:22:51.150
You're right, Foster.

00:22:51.910 --> 00:22:52.730
Much too far.

00:23:18.550 --> 00:23:19.510
Call 2-9 to moon base.

00:23:20.150 --> 00:23:20.890
Go ahead, turn on.

00:23:23.260 --> 00:23:23.540
Second.

00:23:25.400 --> 00:23:25.640
Roger.

00:23:51.590 --> 00:23:52.390
It's three seconds.

00:23:53.540 --> 00:23:54.260
Re-entry angle.

00:23:54.630 --> 00:23:57.250
5.73 degrees, confirmed.

00:24:00.220 --> 00:24:01.370
Firm entry angle.

00:24:40.900 --> 00:24:41.580
Stay on 2-9.

00:24:43.720 --> 00:24:45.120
Two nines re-entry angles, Eric.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:00.980
Thank you.

00:25:02.680 --> 00:25:03.980
Paula, just re-entry angle.

00:25:04.250 --> 00:25:05.070
Cut back to five.

00:25:15.350 --> 00:25:17.690
If he doesn't adjust, he'll bounce off the Earth's atmosphere out into space.

00:27:12.860 --> 00:27:17.000
Foster? Foster here, I'm happy to say.

00:27:18.060 --> 00:27:18.500
Congratulations.

00:27:20.380 --> 00:27:24.800
Don't let my delight at your survival blind you to the fact that we have a few matters to discuss.

00:28:36.680 --> 00:28:36.900
Oh.

00:28:37.100 --> 00:28:39.220
You've gone too far this time, Straker.

00:28:40.300 --> 00:28:41.280
I don't see it that way.

00:28:41.580 --> 00:28:42.840
You authorize a lunar flight.

00:28:43.660 --> 00:28:44.680
I authorize nothing.

00:28:46.280 --> 00:28:46.880
Looks pretty good.

00:28:47.180 --> 00:28:48.100
I don't want to argue with you.

00:28:49.190 --> 00:28:50.810
You are responsible, whatever the circumstances.

00:28:51.110 --> 00:28:51.550
I agree.

00:28:52.940 --> 00:28:56.840
But Colonel Foster has proved that there is alien interference with our interorbital flights.

00:28:57.520 --> 00:28:58.000
Has he?

00:28:58.730 --> 00:28:59.150
Yes.

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:01.360
And I almost got killed doing it.

00:29:01.820 --> 00:29:02.540
So you say?

00:29:02.800 --> 00:29:03.940
Yes, I say!

00:29:23.670 --> 00:29:24.050
My apologies.

00:29:29.560 --> 00:29:29.880
Thank you.

00:29:32.710 --> 00:29:34.790
I think it's time we laid our cards on the table, Anderson.

00:29:36.300 --> 00:29:36.640
All right?

00:29:38.120 --> 00:29:40.100
I'll tell you what I think of Colonel Forster's so-called proof.

00:29:41.930 --> 00:29:44.890
You knew the commission was going to turn down your space junk clearance program.

00:29:46.020 --> 00:29:47.540
So you instructed Foster to make this flight.

00:29:48.260 --> 00:29:49.200
Now, why should I do that?

00:29:49.380 --> 00:29:50.800
Because you are desperate for evidence.

00:29:51.690 --> 00:29:52.070
Go on.

00:29:52.840 --> 00:29:54.660
You authorize the flight to rig this information.

00:29:55.590 --> 00:29:56.570
But you won't get away with it.

00:29:57.860 --> 00:29:59.500
The Commission convenes the day after tomorrow.

00:30:01.400 --> 00:30:02.800
By the time I get through...

00:30:03.700 --> 00:30:04.740
You'll be out of a job.

00:30:07.450 --> 00:30:07.850
at all.

00:30:09.780 --> 00:30:10.860
I'll see you at the commission meeting.

00:30:19.740 --> 00:30:20.860
Indeed you will, Commander.

00:30:30.310 --> 00:30:31.090
Can he really do it?

00:30:34.540 --> 00:30:35.000
Do what?

00:30:35.980 --> 00:30:36.700
Ease you out.

00:30:38.760 --> 00:30:39.260
I can try.

00:30:43.880 --> 00:30:44.620
What about our evidence?

00:30:45.000 --> 00:30:46.060
They've got to take notice of that.

00:30:46.310 --> 00:30:46.770
Evidence

00:30:48.710 --> 00:30:53.770
What's it going to look like when Henderson claims that we manufactured it just to get a space clearance program?

00:30:57.800 --> 00:30:58.760
But we're right.

00:31:00.600 --> 00:31:02.810
Sometimes, Colonel, that's not quite enough.

00:31:15.000 --> 00:31:15.080
Thank you.

00:31:35.690 --> 00:31:37.450
The tracking data's been processed, sir.

00:31:37.670 --> 00:31:37.950
Anything?

00:31:38.540 --> 00:31:39.360
Not that we can see.

00:31:41.450 --> 00:31:42.470
I should have been able to pick up something.

00:31:43.270 --> 00:31:46.130
There's nothing on Colonel Foster's log except a record of manoeuvres.

00:31:48.780 --> 00:31:50.140
All right, send it down to Shadow Headquarters.

00:31:53.770 --> 00:31:54.410
So what do we do now?

00:31:54.920 --> 00:31:55.600
Any suggestions?

00:31:56.080 --> 00:31:56.380
No.

00:31:56.970 --> 00:31:57.870
But we can't just sit around.

00:31:58.160 --> 00:32:00.000
I've solved quite a few problems by just...

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:02.860
Heading around, as you call it, Colonel, I suggest you try it yourself sometime.

00:32:03.060 --> 00:32:06.080
Commander, the tracking report on Colonel Foster's fight has just come in from moon base.

00:32:06.560 --> 00:32:06.920
And?

00:32:07.920 --> 00:32:08.840
Nothing unusual, sir.

00:32:11.890 --> 00:32:12.050
All right.

00:32:16.450 --> 00:32:17.490
It's the MV3 detector.

00:32:17.750 --> 00:32:19.510
Yes, they're processing the data now.

00:32:20.030 --> 00:32:21.570
Well, we haven't had much luck so far.

00:32:22.190 --> 00:32:23.130
Maybe we're due for a break.

00:32:40.110 --> 00:32:41.290
The MV3 data, sir.

00:32:41.610 --> 00:32:42.110
Ah, thank you.

00:32:42.250 --> 00:32:52.190
Looks like an SPS rocket of some sort.

00:32:53.320 --> 00:32:55.420
Like the limpet rockets used in debris destruction.

00:32:55.780 --> 00:32:58.180
Yeah, but it doesn't make sense.

00:32:59.060 --> 00:32:59.980
I mean, why would the aliens...

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:05.940
put a device like this into earth orbit could be programmed to attack moonship flights blockade

00:33:05.940 --> 00:33:19.330
on moon base maybe why hasn't our radar picked it up base debris it's based in one of those

00:33:19.330 --> 00:33:29.610
burnt out rockets over there well assuming you're right which one could it be considering maddox

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:35.580
practically identical flight paths it would have to be one of these two here

00:33:35.580 --> 00:33:47.740
or Apollo 8 here or B-47. Four possibilities. I think we're on to something.

00:34:09.790 --> 00:34:10.270
It should be okay.

00:34:13.160 --> 00:34:13.480
Freeman!

00:34:14.010 --> 00:34:15.800
Fleck, an assignment for you.

00:34:16.320 --> 00:34:17.860
I want you to launch the interceptors.

00:34:18.550 --> 00:34:18.770
Mission?

00:34:19.500 --> 00:34:21.180
Destroy four pieces of space junk.

00:34:22.030 --> 00:34:24.570
I'll have control relay the coordinates direct to the astronauts.

00:34:25.110 --> 00:34:26.450
You mean space junk in Earth orbit?

00:34:26.930 --> 00:34:27.210
Right.

00:34:27.960 --> 00:34:29.900
I mean use all three interceptors.

00:34:30.160 --> 00:34:45.120
all three yes i know keep moon base undefended nevertheless do it alec once now wait a minute

00:34:45.120 --> 00:34:53.410
do you know what's gonna happen when henderson finds out about this ah yes henderson why don't

00:34:53.410 --> 00:34:59.770
you go over and tell him colonel what he'll go berserk yes

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:07.400
take a nice slow drive give me about half an hour i hope you know what you're doing

00:35:27.520 --> 00:35:29.980
control to intercept a leader steer pro

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:31.580
Programmed course to Earth orbit.

00:35:32.220 --> 00:35:34.360
Receive destruct details from Earth Control.

00:35:34.880 --> 00:35:35.020
Out.

00:35:51.860 --> 00:35:55.700
Miss Eland, when James Henderson calls, tell him I'm unavailable.

00:35:56.100 --> 00:35:57.380
And when he arrives, sir?

00:35:57.840 --> 00:35:58.660
Show him right in.

00:35:58.900 --> 00:35:59.800
The red carpet treatment.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:03.020
He's a very important man. You can expect him at 3 o'clock.

00:36:05.120 --> 00:36:15.640
I want to see Straker immediately.

00:36:15.920 --> 00:36:20.480
And before you try to fob me up with some damn fool excuse, I'm telling you I won't take no for an answer.

00:36:20.920 --> 00:36:24.770
Well, of course you may see him, Mr. Henderson. He's expecting you. Go straight in.

00:36:25.420 --> 00:36:26.920
Oh, thank you.

00:36:30.490 --> 00:36:35.490
Ah, Henderson, you're late. Won't keep you a moment. Studio business.

00:36:37.520 --> 00:36:45.020
Well, I think it's a great script, Mr. Steiner. There we are. Cleared for shooting.

00:36:45.820 --> 00:36:48.680
Thanks. You know, I like the way you operate.

00:36:48.860 --> 00:36:49.460
Oh, thank you.

00:36:49.600 --> 00:36:52.960
Your policy of non-interference. Some executives crawl all over you.

00:36:53.500 --> 00:36:55.880
Well, I can assure you, Mr. Steiner, you'll see very little of me.

00:36:56.000 --> 00:36:59.040
And I'll give you a film the studio will be proud of. Thanks again.

00:37:01.820 --> 00:37:02.280
Nice guy.

00:37:03.230 --> 00:37:03.690
Goodbye.

00:37:04.370 --> 00:37:04.550
Bye.

00:37:09.850 --> 00:37:11.860
Straker, you know I never touch them.

00:37:12.060 --> 00:37:12.880
Voice identification.

00:37:16.240 --> 00:37:17.120
James Henderson.

00:37:18.320 --> 00:37:19.260
Identification positive.

00:37:19.860 --> 00:37:21.060
Henderson James L.

00:37:22.520 --> 00:37:22.800
Thank you.

00:37:43.980 --> 00:37:44.940
I tried to call you, Commander.

00:37:45.180 --> 00:37:46.710
I was told you were not available.

00:37:47.710 --> 00:37:48.350
Are they your instructions?

00:37:48.900 --> 00:37:49.220
Yes.

00:37:50.190 --> 00:37:50.450
I see.

00:37:51.600 --> 00:37:52.840
Very high-handed attitude.

00:37:53.490 --> 00:37:54.350
However, one more question.

00:37:55.610 --> 00:37:59.970
Is it true you ordered all three moon base interceptors to destroy certain items of...

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:08.980
space junk? Correct. Do you realize what you've done? You tell me. You've blatantly and openly

00:38:08.980 --> 00:38:13.240
defied the Commission and left Moonbase and the Earth defenseless. It was my decision. I realized

00:38:13.240 --> 00:38:17.910
the implications. You had better start packing, Straker. When the Commission hears about this,

00:38:17.970 --> 00:38:22.780
you're through. Aren't you interested in hearing my reasons? No, let's be kind. Let's put it down

00:38:22.780 --> 00:38:28.090
to a mental aberration, the strain of command. Get those interceptors back on Moonbase, Commander,

00:38:28.270 --> 00:38:29.150
while you can still give orders.

00:38:31.120 --> 00:38:31.800
Sorry, Henderson.

00:38:32.260 --> 00:38:33.720
Don't push your luck, Straker.

00:38:33.960 --> 00:38:37.490
If Moonbase reports a UFO sighting, stick around.

00:38:39.260 --> 00:38:40.120
I'm expecting it.

00:39:26.910 --> 00:39:29.470
Contact 248-016.

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:37.800
Red. Contact confirmed. UFO 248-136. Red.

00:39:37.980 --> 00:39:40.010
Red alert. Get me Shadow Headquarters.

00:39:41.000 --> 00:39:42.800
UFO maintaining 4...

00:39:45.160 --> 00:39:45.940
Get the termination.

00:39:47.500 --> 00:39:48.960
Request trajectory termination.

00:39:49.740 --> 00:39:50.260
Termination.

00:39:53.360 --> 00:39:56.620
Close enough. Target is this studio.

00:39:58.320 --> 00:39:59.920
Maintain visual contact on countdown.

00:40:00.060 --> 00:40:00.140
We'll be right back.

00:40:00.570 --> 00:40:00.930
Yes, sir.

00:40:01.910 --> 00:40:03.070
And order a complete shutdown.

00:40:03.470 --> 00:40:03.950
Shutdown?

00:40:04.150 --> 00:40:04.610
Everything.

00:40:04.890 --> 00:40:06.390
VHF, radar, the computers.

00:40:06.870 --> 00:40:07.990
Complete radio silence.

00:40:08.410 --> 00:40:08.810
Stryker!

00:40:09.180 --> 00:40:10.880
As you said, Henderson, I can still give orders.

00:40:11.740 --> 00:40:12.360
Complete shutdown.

00:40:13.400 --> 00:40:13.760
Do it.

00:40:25.240 --> 00:40:25.700
Termination.

00:40:26.490 --> 00:40:27.090
Eight minutes.

00:40:27.670 --> 00:40:28.210
Four seconds.

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:30.320
Thank you.

00:40:31.050 --> 00:40:32.030
Thank you.

00:40:36.970 --> 00:40:37.290
Thank you.

00:40:39.850 --> 00:40:40.230
And let's drink it.

00:40:40.840 --> 00:40:41.820
I'd like to talk to you in your office.

00:40:43.940 --> 00:40:44.460
You too, Cuddle.

00:41:00.630 --> 00:41:00.950
Drinker!

00:41:01.880 --> 00:41:03.080
I'm relieving you of your command.

00:41:03.860 --> 00:41:05.580
Colonel Foster will take over as of now.

00:41:05.760 --> 00:41:06.540
You can't do it, Henderson.

00:41:06.820 --> 00:41:08.580
You require the unanimous backing of the commission.

00:41:08.800 --> 00:41:09.880
You think I won't get it?

00:41:10.020 --> 00:41:11.100
Yes, I think you could get it.

00:41:11.580 --> 00:41:12.420
But it would take time.

00:41:12.760 --> 00:41:14.540
And this base is due to be attacked in a few minutes.

00:41:15.990 --> 00:41:16.550
Colonel Forster?

00:41:17.240 --> 00:41:17.960
Assume command.

00:41:20.950 --> 00:41:21.230
Pedal.

00:41:24.220 --> 00:41:25.760
I take my orders from Commander Straker.

00:41:28.340 --> 00:41:29.980
Now, for the first time in your life, Henry,

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:31.060
You're going to listen.

00:41:32.520 --> 00:41:36.140
The aliens put a satellite into Earth orbit, using a piece of space junk to cover.

00:41:36.840 --> 00:41:37.180
Why?

00:41:37.960 --> 00:41:39.120
A blockade on Moonbase?

00:41:39.910 --> 00:41:41.250
A logical reason, but obvious.

00:41:41.740 --> 00:41:42.280
Too obvious.

00:41:42.730 --> 00:41:44.530
In time, we would have located and destroyed it.

00:41:45.450 --> 00:41:46.930
So the satellite was a decoy.

00:41:47.660 --> 00:41:49.040
A red herring for something bigger.

00:41:50.090 --> 00:41:51.270
An attack on this headquarters.

00:41:52.230 --> 00:41:54.630
They hoped the satellite would draw the interceptors for moon base.

00:41:56.620 --> 00:41:58.480
And you fell right into the trap.

00:41:58.620 --> 00:41:59.920
I acted as if the plan had worked.

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:00.320
Yes.

00:42:02.100 --> 00:42:05.660
It would take a UFO of great destructive power to destroy this underground base.

00:42:05.860 --> 00:42:07.660
I didn't want that hanging over our heads.

00:42:09.750 --> 00:42:12.110
All this guesswork does not explain the shutdown.

00:42:12.390 --> 00:42:13.490
Why make it easy for them?

00:42:13.850 --> 00:42:16.330
The UFO is probably programmed onto our radio signals.

00:42:16.790 --> 00:42:17.930
I don't buy it, Stryker.

00:42:19.100 --> 00:42:20.560
I just hope you've guessed wrong.

00:42:21.340 --> 00:42:22.060
Because if you're right,

00:42:22.810 --> 00:42:23.650
We're about to be killed.

00:42:36.300 --> 00:42:37.320
Still time for you to leave.

00:42:42.470 --> 00:42:42.790
All right.

00:42:43.820 --> 00:42:45.120
We all just sit here and wait.

00:42:45.390 --> 00:42:45.930
For what?

00:42:47.340 --> 00:42:47.760
A voice.

00:42:58.700 --> 00:42:59.940
Moonbase to shadow control.

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:01.820
Control. Come in, Control.

00:43:04.470 --> 00:43:06.930
It's no use, sir. It's a complete radio shutdown.

00:43:07.210 --> 00:43:09.490
What the hell is Stryker playing at?

00:43:14.190 --> 00:43:15.650
Four minutes to termination.

00:43:17.300 --> 00:43:20.340
Stryker, if we contact the interceptors, there may still be time.

00:43:21.000 --> 00:43:23.580
It's no good. They can't operate in the Earth's atmosphere.

00:43:24.310 --> 00:43:25.730
And the UFO's already in the stratosphere.

00:43:28.220 --> 00:43:29.560
Termination. One minute...

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:30.420
20 seconds.

00:43:35.300 --> 00:43:36.000
We're sitting ducks.

00:43:37.100 --> 00:43:37.400
Maybe.

00:43:56.840 --> 00:43:57.040
Yes.

00:44:00.860 --> 00:44:01.560
Thank you, Ms. Eland.

00:44:03.110 --> 00:44:03.870
Switch everything on.

00:44:04.090 --> 00:44:04.430
Yes, sir.

00:44:05.910 --> 00:44:06.910
And get me Captain Carlin.

00:44:07.760 --> 00:44:07.940
Sir.

00:44:12.400 --> 00:44:13.140
Nice timing, Captain.

00:44:13.780 --> 00:44:14.420
Don't miss it.

00:44:14.730 --> 00:44:15.270
Roger control.

00:44:16.600 --> 00:44:17.660
Sky one to moon base.

00:44:18.160 --> 00:44:20.020
Quest UFO fix and attack coordinates.

00:44:20.510 --> 00:44:22.330
We'll relay direct to outward computer.

00:44:25.180 --> 00:44:26.720
Breaking a sly old...

00:44:26.940 --> 00:44:27.320
Fox?

00:44:28.590 --> 00:44:29.370
45 seconds.

00:44:33.230 --> 00:44:42.900
40 seconds, 35 seconds, 30 seconds.

00:44:52.260 --> 00:44:54.320
Have visual contact. Going in for attack.

00:45:12.570 --> 00:45:15.080
Shatter control, UFO destroyed.

00:45:23.400 --> 00:45:28.800
Foster, to get this operation computerized and we'll prepare it for the commission in my office.

00:45:39.950 --> 00:45:42.970
Well, Straker, I guess I owe you an apology. You were right.

00:45:46.980 --> 00:45:49.960
You can take it. The commission will recommend a complete clearance of all space junk.

00:45:51.020 --> 00:45:51.300
Thank you.

00:45:53.070 --> 00:45:55.350
Of course, it'll take time. The money has to be raised.

00:45:56.950 --> 00:45:57.870
Call it the Maddox Fund.

00:45:58.800 --> 00:45:59.120
Maddox?

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:08.240
was killed yes max well if only you hadn't been so positive that you were

00:46:08.240 --> 00:46:21.010
right like you Henderson give me your car

00:47:01.340 --> 00:47:01.560
You
